      "requiredInCI": true,
      "ciStep": "backend-foundations-guard"
    },
    {
      "id": "test-execution-integrity",
      "script": "tools/agent-hooks/check-test-execution-integrity.mjs",
      "makeTarget": "test-execution-integrity-guard",
      "realCheck": "node tools/agent-hooks/check-test-execution-integrity.mjs",
      "selfTest": "node tools/agent-hooks/check-test-execution-integrity.mjs --self-test",
      "owningDoc": "docs/engineering/backend-go-postgres-quality.md",
      "requiredInCI": true,
      "ciStep": "test-execution-integrity-guard",
      "notes": "Detects Go test files with stray build constraints (// +build pgtest, //go:build pgtest, etc.) that cause them to be silently excluded from CI runs. Postgres tests must gate at runtime via GOATOS_RUN_POSTGRES_TESTS=1 + pgtest.SkipIfNoDocker(), not via build tags."
    },
    {
      "id": "operator-cap-fail-closed",
      "script": "tools/agent-hooks/check-operator-cap-fail-closed.mjs",
      "makeTarget": "operator-cap-fail-closed-guard",
      "realCheck": "node tools/agent-hooks/check-operator-cap-fail-closed.mjs",
      "selfTest": "node tools/agent-hooks/check-operator-cap-fail-closed.mjs --self-test",
      "owningDoc": "docs/decisions/scale-anti-patterns.md",
      "requiredInCI": true,
      "ciStep": "operator-cap-fail-closed-guard",
      "notes": "Detects callers of operatorCapacityPlanner / effectiveOperatorAnimalCap in backend/internal/obligation/app/** that feed the returned cap into a capacity limit/lock sink without a fail-closed check (driveOperatorCapacityExhausted, or maxDriveCells>0 && effectiveCap<=0), which reintroduces the F1 fail-open (cap<=0 read as uncapped) on a config-present-but-no-executable-operator day."
    },
    {
      "id": "cascade-event-wiring",
      "script": "tools/agent-hooks/check-cascade-event-wiring.mjs",
      "makeTarget": "cascade-event-wiring-guard",
      "realCheck": "node tools/agent-hooks/check-cascade-event-wiring.mjs",
      "selfTest": "node tools/agent-hooks/check-cascade-event-wiring.mjs --self-test",
      "owningDoc": "docs/decisions/scale-anti-patterns.md",
      "requiredInCI": true,
      "ciStep": "cascade-event-wiring-guard",
      "notes": "Blocks the three operator-cascade wiring anti-patterns proven broken at origin/main f9a44b84: (B) an eventbus handler type with Register(bus eventbus.Bus) that is missing from a DURABLE bus (backend/internal/kernelstages/bus.go and backend/cmd/domain-event-consumer/main.go) while being registered only on bootstrap/api.go or domainconsumer/wiring/bus.go, which nothing real dispatches to; (A) a sweeper function consuming DB-reported operator.Cap without subtracting session.vaccinationOperatorLoad, which lets a later rule-version in the same sweep over-select past the per-operator/day cap; (C) a write to workforce_positions cap/week-off, vaccination_capacity_config, or vaccination_operator_assignment_config that never enqueues vaccination.capacity.changed / vaccination.roster.changed. Deliberate durable-bus omissions must be declared in DURABLE_BUS_EXEMPTIONS with a written reason, and the guard re-verifies that the exemption's declared registration site still registers the handler."
    },
